[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Create `projects/<project-slug>/planning/runbook-generation-quality-gate.md`
[stderr] and validation instructions/scripts that can be run after every B-series wave.
[stderr] Validate the authoring collection itself and the R-series contracts it produces.
[stderr] The validation is structural and traceability-based; it must not claim the
[stderr] product has been implemented or released.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Validation checks required front matter, unique IDs, sequence ordering,
[stderr]   requirement links, dependency closure, output ownership, and unsupported
[stderr]   circular dependencies. Every R contract must also have non-empty provenance:
[stderr]   canonical `source_specifications`, `source_catalogue_ids`, its originating
[stderr]   `authoring_batch`, and valid `factory_stages`; the links must resolve to the
[stderr]   manifest and canonical specification rather than merely naming an F or B
[stderr]   procedure file.
[stderr] - Validation checks every R-series contract has an explicit asset assessment:
[stderr]   `asset_impact` is `required` or `not_applicable`, `asset_ids` is present,
[stderr]   asset-required contracts reserve non-empty unique stable IDs and an asset
[stderr]   brief/style version, and non-asset contracts do not silently introduce asset
[stderr]   work. It reports missing, duplicate, ambiguous, or unowned asset IDs.
[stderr] - It detects duplicate browser test paths and confirms browser-impact metadata
[stderr]   only where browser behaviour is actually in scope.
[stderr] - It reports catalogue/manifest/specification coverage counts and identifies
[stderr]   every missing, duplicate, blocked, or unverified contract by ID.
[stderr] - It fails the quality gate when a discovered domain family has no specification
[stderr]   chapter, content/authoring approach where applicable, implementation
[stderr]   contracts, or traceable verification. It checks category-appropriate
[stderr]   completeness rather than applying a fixed checklist to every product.
[stderr] - It includes recovery: how to rerun one failed B-series authoring task, repair
[stderr]   a bounded R-series range, and resume the next dispatcher wave without
[stderr]   regenerating accepted work.
[stderr] - Human gates, paid services, credentials, legal/compliance decisions, device
[stderr]   access, and store/certification actions remain explicit review points.
