[stderr] +# Runbook-generation quality gate
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Run this after each B-series authoring wave:
[stderr] +
[stderr] +```zsh
[stderr] +python3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py
[stderr] +```
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Use `--wave B0004` for a checkpoint through one batch. The validator reads the
[stderr] +canonical specification, catalogue, manifest, B writers, and generated R
[stderr] +contracts. It is structural evidence only: it does not build, test, review,
[stderr] +deploy, or release the product.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Checks
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- Unique, ordered B/R IDs; dependency closure/cycles; manifest output ownership;
[stderr] +  requirement links; and exact, canonical provenance links.
[stderr] +- Required R front matter (including `requirement_ids`) and matching manifest
[stderr] +  metadata, an explicit Asset assessment section, and verification ownership.
[stderr] +  Missing, duplicate, blocked, unverified, and unallocated IDs are printed with
[stderr] +  catalogue, manifest, and specification coverage counts.
[stderr] +- Explicit asset assessments. Asset-required work needs unique stable `ASSET-*`
[stderr] +  IDs, an asset brief, and a visual-style version; non-asset work may not reserve
[stderr] +  IDs or silently introduce asset work.
[stderr] +- Unique browser test paths and browser-impact metadata only for web/PWA
[stderr] +  behaviour. A web/PWA target alone does not require browser metadata.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The initial foundation wave correctly fails until B writers create their
[stderr] +reserved R files; that is a missing authoring artefact, not product failure.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Recovery and human review
[stderr] +
[stderr] +1. Rerun only the failed B writer using its manifest context packet; retain its
[stderr] +   B/R IDs and change only assigned R paths.
[stderr] +2. Repair a bounded R range through its owning B writer(s), then rerun this
[stderr] +   command through the final affected `--wave` value. Never regenerate accepted
[stderr] +   work or renumber IDs.
[stderr] +3. Checkpoint accepted work and resume the dispatcher at the manifest's first
[stderr] +   unaccepted B batch.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Stop for human review on gates, credentials, paid services, legal/compliance or
[stderr] +licensing decisions, device access, store/certification actions, deployment,
[stderr] +publishing, or release approval. Mark work blocked and retain IDs.
